  "details": "With the huge rave scene, and all the people who love audio on the platform, it seems like a good faith feature to make 128 kb/s, currently it seems to be using an non recommended means of audio handling, along with the lowest possible audio quality overhead before things sound really crunchy, This has nothing to do with the spacial audio system vrchat is using, Simply the networking side of the audio pipeline. \n\nIt seems that vrchat is using 30kb/s Audio instead of an acceptable 128 kb/s. \n\nThis causes a lot of cut outs and audio degradation compared to other platforms, as it seems to be using a 30kb buss for audio on client side. at least it seams that way on audio output, across multiple devices.",
